   "body": "A fix is on [the fork branch](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/5708-tray-motion-reduced-inflight), commit [1184f194d](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/1184f194d4d9790d5b0077b6c9299db7dca3ac24), based on `ed0ab567`.\n\nWith motion reduced (system setting or magpie's Settings toggle, which share one `calm()` check), an in-flight request used to read as finished because the stage's markers had their animations off and `pPlay` bailed out early. Now `pPlay` still draws the dot, and the reduce media block plays opacity-only versions: `ps-wait` for the waiting dot, the row arrow and the destination dot, and a small opacity pulse for the busy hub. Nothing scales or changes geometry on the reduce path, and the motion-on CSS is unchanged.\n\nVerified through CDP against the built assets with both emulated media states: the reduce path resolves to the opacity keyframes and every marker's computed `transform` is `none`, opacity samples captured while running; the no-preference control still shows the scale animation. `go vet`, the offline `nogui` build and `git diff --check` pass. Not covered: the full `?mode=panel` client pipeline in a browser, WebKit, and a visual run with motion on. AI-assisted implementation and review.",
